#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553677} :activity/id #uuid "02ab6ed4-47f1-525b-9777-cf24c2343051" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050054 :topic/id #uuid "29ce72ae-dbea-5d83-a81d-90545461cdec" :topic/math-academy-id 6375} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553597 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e5577e5-b719-5b3f-b68d-1a75b4f32803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306635} :answer-field/id #uuid "44dfc463-2eed-5b8f-a49b-1a3832e8c840" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0a7c5d9-d376-5bfc-a898-b72ac7a7d83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186307230} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a80531-ea9b-5f87-832d-76058c53931d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b1ecd54-364c-5cc5-a146-14c0aa79943d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306024} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f4d138-3d8f-5af5-bab0-3f349b34eb48" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c31d763-cb9f-53cb-b3d1-d640d1818379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305410} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb057fc7-7654-5c34-bfa6-3eaa85ee1200" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d14a11c3-0a49-5696-a62c-af65df34be1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335108" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0b4cefa4-af80-5c7c-83a1-ff4d5ac31dcb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7afe076b-ab10-5a6d-92ee-d9bda36095eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370131} :answer-field/id #uuid "8717736e-bf1d-56b9-8978-2ee27ddc1c10" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370130} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116b716d-7743-526a-8367-67bb770fa2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370133} :answer-field/id #uuid "6684d3cf-4512-5e44-a922-9538752b4a1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "eace89bb-5f6d-586f-b6ba-d2d1f4b38da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-334633" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm \\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & -{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot \\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\frac{1}{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "16872273-54fb-5073-a5e6-85ee3dbf9ea6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553611}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553611 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cddbd6d-ffb7-5530-be33-109a25cb590f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305736} :answer-field/id #uuid "28239443-16fd-5045-bb7b-a3e946af529a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fff644e-a154-526d-b37a-e4f82a475e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306218} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cec750e-1b50-5e87-b62d-239edf61a752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d74b37d0-1ddd-5304-877c-4617a1e8ae03" :question/math-academy-id "q-334735" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $3,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\,\\,$ |  | $1+4t$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $8t$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & -2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 8{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(3t) &={e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n3t{e}^{3t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{3t}(1-3t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-2{e}^{3t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(-2t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{3t}t+{e}^{3t}(1-3t) \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}(1-4t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{3t}\\begin{bmatrix}1+4t & -2t \\\\ 8t & 1-4t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "30faf73f-f8c2-56a2-805f-6ce1667a314c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71d01b6-ee5b-5054-8b30-0826abc684a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+2t)e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553358} :answer-field/id #uuid "9199806a-56d9-516c-b5c9-c3a184f8a0be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220637} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8adba1a9-ea42-59fb-9093-1e1960d724e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553150}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553150} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd89e18-df1a-52e5-b1a9-13b9a350e74e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79588b6e-67a9-51cd-86b3-3db3fa8e6c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553116} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d46c25a-b0e5-5cb8-b4d9-bcfcbeae85f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f1d256-cbeb-55b4-a0df-384c213379d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553295}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553295} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c309815-d4c5-5708-9d45-6e7c0e1436e3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220640}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e415201f-e8d7-5cac-99e4-ae2f79b7e01e" :question/math-academy-id "q-333858" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2t} & (2t+1){e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e0e6cc77-900e-5194-bf84-c2fa20bd1df9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553601}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553504 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8abba599-d405-5b28-8292-a43ed4750a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553149}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553149} :answer-field/id #uuid "03ccd2db-1552-543e-9102-8cfc8d2f158f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9e4d7af-e293-52fb-87b2-17e379489288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553364} :answer-field/id #uuid "416cdcae-3262-544e-a6bf-81a343fec464" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23c462cc-da9f-5356-aacb-68452f1af0c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-334736" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\n*Hint: The only eigenvalue of $A$ is $-2,$ and it has multiplicity two.*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${e}^{At}={e}^{-2t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">$1-4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$1+4t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -8{\\alpha }_{1}t & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-2t)={e}^{-2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-2t)={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}(-2t){\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-2t{e}^{-2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}(1+2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2{e}^{-2t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(2t) \\\\ -8{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-8{e}^{-2t}t \\\\  & ={e}^{-2t}(-8t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1-4t & 2t \\\\ -8t & 1+4t\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eb5fe771-6cf7-59f9-a5b4-123061340a58" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553597}}] :activity/title "Matrix Exponentials" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552851}]}
